# The Madaros witness set.
#
# CI runs lean_single. Every check that exists is therefore blind to the
# modular Madaros compiler, which is what `bin/souc` actually resolves to and
# what users get. That gap is not theoretical: on 2026-08-21 the default engine
# could not bind `let d: mg = 500.0` at all, refused a correct refinement alias
# and an incorrect one with the SAME diagnostic, and carried a live
# first-order-variance regression on main that no check reported.
#
# The full corpus cannot close it. 1773 programs serialised exceed the
# 60-minute CI limit; parallel, the raw ELF SIGSEGVs under memory pressure and
# invents regressions. A corpus is a periodic Slurm sweep, not a per-PR gate.
#
# This is the per-PR gate instead: a small set, built from source, covering the
# things lean_single structurally cannot see. Each entry must carry
# `//@ expect-stdout:` or `//@ error-pattern:` so a wrong ANSWER fails, not
# merely a crash.
#
# One path per line. Keep it small enough that build + run stays well inside
# the CI budget. Add an entry when a Madaros-only defect is found; that is what
# makes the set grow for a reason.

# first-order GUM variance across calls.
#
# KNOWN FAILING on main as of 2026-08-21, and left in the set on purpose.
# Both print 0.000000 where a variance is expected -- v5s, v5p, v8s, vw. The
# defect predates this set: a witness run at eb91a600ef, the commit BEFORE the
# i256/i512 work, fails identically, and so does clean main. It is the
# long-recorded "FO variance dies across a call" defect, not a regression.
#
# They are listed with `!` so the gate counts them as known and stays green on
# today's truth, and goes red the day ANOTHER witness breaks. Removing them
# would hide the only in-CI record that this is broken; leaving them unmarked
# would make the gate permanently red, which is a dead gate within a week.
#
# Drop the `!` when the defect is fixed. That is the whole ratchet.
!tests/run-pass/madaros_gum_fo_eight_param.sio
!tests/run-pass/madaros_gum_fo_mutual.sio

# dimensional analysis -- dead under Madaros until 2026-08-21
tests/run-pass/unit_scalar_mul.sio
tests/compile-fail/unit_cast_incompatible.sio
tests/compile-fail/unit_literal_absorbs_not_computed.sio

# provenance -- a computed value may not claim it was obtained
tests/compile-fail/r_origin_measured_on_sum.sio
tests/run-pass/r_origin_derived_on_sum.sio
tests/run-pass/r_origin_measured_on_call_is_silent.sio

# wide integers -- i256/i512 limb multiply against the Lorenz oracle
tests/run-pass/r1_i256_lorenz_peak.sio
tests/run-pass/r1_i512_lorenz_peak.sio
